CHAPTER FOUR
PROJECT OUTCOMES, MARKETING, FINANCIAL ANALYSIS AND SUSTAINABILITY
4.0 Introduction
This chapter presents the outcomes of the Climate-Smart Improved Kienyeji Chicken Broiler Production Enterprise implemented by the Form Four Agriculture candidates of St. Mary's Girls Secondary School – Thigio. It evaluates the performance of the enterprise, marketing strategies adopted, financial performance, value addition opportunities, environmental sustainability, lessons learnt, recommendations, and the overall success of the project.
The project was undertaken to demonstrate practical poultry production skills while addressing local challenges such as high feed costs, disease outbreaks, water scarcity, and the effects of climate change.
